WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.330
In 2004, a tsunami struck Kuala
Cangkoy, a village in Aceh.

2
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.720
Oxfam reported in 2005 that,
for every male who died,

3
00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:11.810
4 females died.

4
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:18.930
In Cuddalore, in India, 391
women died, against 146 men.

5
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.130
Was it random?

6
00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:21.990
Were only the men warned?

7
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.230
Why would a wave choose?

8
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.690
In this mission, you'll break
disaster risk into four parts:

9
00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:32.530
hazard, exposure,
vulnerability and capacity.

10
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.550
Then you'll weigh economic, social,
political and geographic factors,

11
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.470
and test two models of how
vulnerability builds up.

12
00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:45.570
Your mission: explain why the same wave
killed far more females than males in

13
00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:46.760
Kuala Cangkoy.
